---
import QuestionLayout from '@layouts/QuestionLayout.astro';

const relatedLinks = [];
const _body = "<p>The Traverse CLI is the <code>traverse</code> command-line tool you use to compile contracts, register capabilities, execute them locally, and inspect results. It is published on crates.io as <code>traverse-cli-rs</code> (the installed binary is <code>traverse-cli</code>) and wraps the full runtime in a developer-friendly interface.</p>\n\n      <h2>What you can do with it</h2>\n      <ul>\n        <li>Compile a contract TOML file into a validated contract artifact</li>\n        <li>Register a capability (contract + WASM binary) into the local registry</li>\n        <li>Run a capability with a JSON input and see the output and trace</li>\n        <li>List all registered capabilities and their versions</li>\n        <li>Start the MCP stdio server for AI agent integration</li>\n        <li>Inspect trace artifacts from previous executions</li>\n      </ul>\n\n      <h2>Basic usage</h2>\n      <pre><code># Scaffold a new capability package\ntraverse-cli capability new pricing.calculate-total\n\n# After you build the wasm32-wasip1 binary, register a bundle's\n# capabilities, events, and workflows\ntraverse-cli bundle register examples/expedition/registry-bundle/manifest.json\n\n# Execute a capability package against a runtime request\ntraverse-cli capability-package execute capabilities/pricing.calculate-total/manifest.json request.json\n\n# List registered capabilities\ntraverse-cli registry list</code></pre>\n\n      <h2>Starting the MCP server</h2>\n      <p>The MCP stdio server ships as its own binary, separate from the CLI:</p>\n      <pre><code>traverse-mcp stdio</code></pre>\n      <p>This makes your local registry available to any MCP-compatible client, including Claude Desktop. See <a href=\"/questions/how-does-the-mcp-server-work.html\">how the MCP server works</a> for details.</p>\n\n      <h2>Installation</h2>\n      <p>Install from crates.io with Cargo:</p>\n      <pre><code>cargo install traverse-cli-rs --version =0.15.0 --locked</code></pre>\n      <p>Watch the crate name: <code>traverse-cli</code> on crates.io is an unrelated project (a Solidity analysis tool) that installs a binary with the same name, so <code>cargo install traverse-cli</code> gets you the wrong tool. You need Rust 1.94 or newer (for example <code>rustup toolchain install 1.94.0</code>, then <code>cargo +1.94.0 install traverse-cli-rs --locked</code>) and the <code>wasm32-wasip1</code> target installed. <code>model package-onnx</code> also needs the audited ONNX runner guest, which the crate doesn't bundle: download <code>runner.wasm</code> from the <a href=\"https://github.com/traverse-framework/traverse/releases/tag/onnx-runner-v0.15.0\">onnx-runner-v0.15.0</a> release and check its sha256 (<code>f3902703fe79cc161c13b87cf507dcb25cb53ea3c2a68bed6cc753f9df100966</code>) before you use it (<a href=\"https://github.com/traverse-framework/traverse/issues/1687\">#1687</a>). Walk-through: <a href=\"/questions/how-do-i-package-an-onnx-model-for-traverse.html\">how do I package an ONNX model?</a> See the <a href=\"/docs/cli-reference.html\">CLI reference</a> for a full command listing.</p>";
const _jsonLd = "{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What is the Traverse CLI?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"The Traverse CLI (crate traverse-cli-rs, binary traverse-cli) is the command-line tool for compiling contracts, registering capabilities, running them locally, and inspecting trace artifacts. It is the primary interface for developing with Traverse outside of an IDE.\"}}]}";
---
<QuestionLayout
  title={"What is the Traverse CLI?"}
  description={"The Traverse CLI is the command-line tool for building, registering, and running WASM capabilities. Learn what it does and how to use it."}
  canonical={"https://traverse-framework.com/questions/what-is-the-traverse-cli.html"}
  category={"Getting Started"}
  relatedLinks={relatedLinks}
  jsonLd={_jsonLd}
>
  <Fragment set:html={_body} />
</QuestionLayout>
